{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00216",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 3.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. It's my turn, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.71,
      "end_seconds": 8.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.66,
      "end_seconds": 14.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.59,
      "end_seconds": 18.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.31,
      "end_seconds": 33.47,
      "duration_seconds": 14.16,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got cramping pain in the lower tummy. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.87,
      "end_seconds": 37.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.51,
      "end_seconds": 44.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "I've had it for about a month. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.37,
      "end_seconds": 48.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Right, on a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.68,
      "end_seconds": 54.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.84,
      "end_seconds": 57.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.86,
      "end_seconds": 74.27,
      "duration_seconds": 15.41,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a feeling of not emptying fully as well. The feeling of not emptying fully? That's been for three weeks. About feeling of not emptying fully, a seven out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.26,
      "end_seconds": 78.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.49,
      "end_seconds": 84.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.32,
      "end_seconds": 91.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, fever or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.13,
      "end_seconds": 94.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.88,
      "end_seconds": 99.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Any blood in the stool or family history of bowel cancer?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.52,
      "end_seconds": 101.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.09,
      "end_seconds": 105.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.17,
      "end_seconds": 108.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "No, you know, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.67,
      "end_seconds": 115.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.99,
      "end_seconds": 118.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Alright, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.69,
      "end_seconds": 120.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.85,
      "end_seconds": 125.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.44,
      "end_seconds": 139.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.84,
      "end_seconds": 146.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Right, do you have any known allergies at all? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.17,
      "end_seconds": 147.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.22,
      "end_seconds": 153.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.89,
      "end_seconds": 164.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.61,
      "end_seconds": 173.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.24,
      "end_seconds": 175.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.85,
      "end_seconds": 183.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known acid reflux. We'll keep that in mind today. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 184.82,
      "end_seconds": 190.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "She is on omeprazole, once a day, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.88,
      "end_seconds": 192.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 193.43,
      "end_seconds": 194.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "It's 20 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.95,
      "end_seconds": 208.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.88,
      "end_seconds": 210.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.78,
      "end_seconds": 216.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.42,
      "end_seconds": 219.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.84,
      "end_seconds": 231.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.88,
      "end_seconds": 233.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.8,
      "end_seconds": 260.78,
      "duration_seconds": 23.98,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.19,
      "end_seconds": 263.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.88,
      "end_seconds": 277.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.38,
      "end_seconds": 280.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.1,
      "end_seconds": 303.77,
      "duration_seconds": 19.67,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had cramping pain in the lower tummy for about a month, moderate, and no blood in the stool or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.58,
      "end_seconds": 310.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Right, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.03,
      "end_seconds": 320.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for bowel symptoms. Let's get a stool calprotectin, for bowel symptoms. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.88,
      "end_seconds": 323.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.19,
      "end_seconds": 347.55,
      "duration_seconds": 23.36,
      "text": "I'm prescribing mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day, for four weeks. You take it by mouth. That's for abdominal cramps. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.51,
      "end_seconds": 357.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.58,
      "end_seconds": 362.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.04,
      "end_seconds": 366.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.26,
      "end_seconds": 375.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "So, I take the mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.66,
      "end_seconds": 381.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.17,
      "end_seconds": 384.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.4,
      "end_seconds": 387.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "So, bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}